From 4910c865abb09c6e90f91dffc68f7fbeeb84ff1c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marnick Vandecauter <security@marnick.net>
Date: Sun, 24 May 2026 22:28:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] F101 (hygiene): clear KISS packet buffer in place
 across FEND
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When a CCSDS TM frame contains two or more KISS FEND delimiters, the
code published the first packet correctly, then did
self.packets[vc] = [] which rebound the dict entry to a fresh list.
The local 'packet' variable still pointed at the now-published list,
so bytes between the second FEND and the next publication landed on
the orphan instead of the fresh buffer; the next FEND then published
the orphan's residue.

Net effect: operators decoding ASRTU-1 saw a stale APID-200 beacon
value (temperature, etc.) for one frame after every multi-packet TM.
Real bug but the impact is one stale dashboard value per multi-FEND
frame, not security-significant in any deployed scenario — hygiene
patch, no CVE filed.

Reference: audit finding F101 (gr-satellites v5.9.0 audit, 2026-05-24)
---
 python/components/transports/tm_kiss_transport.py | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/python/components/transports/tm_kiss_transport.py b/python/components/transports/tm_kiss_transport.py
index c69aee7..01c519e 100644
--- a/python/components/transports/tm_kiss_transport.py
+++ b/python/components/transports/tm_kiss_transport.py
@@ -64,7 +64,13 @@ class tm_kiss_transport(gr.basic_block):
                         pmt.intern('out'),
                         pmt.cons(pmt.PMT_NIL,
                                  pmt.init_u8vector(len(packet), packet)))
-                    self.packets[vc] = []
+                    # Audit finding F101: clear the buffer in place rather
+                    # than rebinding the dict entry to a new list. The old
+                    # code did self.packets[vc] = [], which left `packet`
+                    # pointing at the published list; bytes between the
+                    # next FEND and the publication landed on the orphan
+                    # instead of the fresh buffer.
+                    packet.clear()
             elif self.transpose[vc]:
                 if c == TFEND:
                     packet.append(FEND)
